## 3. Walkthrough & Exam Drills

### Drill 1: Rapid Imperative Creation (`01-imperative-creation/`)

In the CKA exam, time is critical. Creating ConfigMaps and Secrets imperatively saves significant time over writing raw
YAML:

#### Step 1: Create from Literal Key-Value Pairs

```bash
kubectl create configmap app-settings \
  --from-literal=APP_ENV=production \
  --from-literal=LOG_LEVEL=info \
  --dry-run=client -o yaml
```

#### Step 2: Create from Individual Files

```bash
# Stores file contents under key matching filename ('app.properties')
kubectl create configmap app-props --from-file=app.properties

# Stores file contents under custom key name ('custom.conf')
kubectl create configmap ui-settings --from-file=custom.conf=ui.conf
```

#### Step 3: Create from Environment Files (`--from-env-file`)

```bash
# Unpacks each LINE in game.env as an individual ConfigMap key
kubectl create configmap game-env-config --from-env-file=game.env
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Notice the key difference: `--from-file=game.env` creates a **single key** named `game.env` containing the entire file
> content, whereas `--from-env-file=game.env` parses each `KEY=VALUE` line into a **distinct top-level key**.

#### Step 4: Corresponding Secret Creation

```bash
kubectl create secret generic db-creds \
  --from-literal=username=dbadmin \
  --from-literal=password='S3cretP@ssword' \
  --dry-run=client -o yaml
```

