### Drill 2: Granular vs. Bulk Environment Variable Injection (`02-env-var-injection/`)

There are two primary patterns to pass configuration data as container environment variables:

#### Step 1: Granular Injection (`valueFrom`)

Inject individual keys into container environment variables, mapping them to arbitrary environment variable names:

```yaml
containers:
  - name: app
    image: busybox:1.36
    env:
      - name: RUNTIME_ENV
        valueFrom:
          configMapKeyRef:
            name: sample-app-config
            key: APP_ENV
      - name: DB_PASSWORD
        valueFrom:
          secretKeyRef:
            name: sample-app-secret
            key: password
```

#### Step 2: Bulk Injection (`envFrom`)

Inject all keys from a ConfigMap or Secret as environment variables in a single declaration. Use an optional `prefix` to
prevent naming collisions:

```yaml
containers:
  - name: app
    image: busybox:1.36
    envFrom:
      - prefix: CFG_
        configMapRef:
          name: sample-app-config
      - secretRef:
        name: sample-app-secret
```

