### Drill 3: Volume Mounts & `subPath` Projections (`03-volume-mounts-subpath/`)

When applications require structured configuration files (e.g. `nginx.conf`, `application.properties`) on disk:

#### Step 1: Full Directory Volume Mount

Mounting a ConfigMap volume mounts every key as a separate file inside the target directory.

```yaml
volumeMounts:
  - name: config-vol
    mountPath: /etc/sample-config
    readOnly: true
volumes:
  - name: config-vol
    configMap:
      name: sample-service-config
      defaultMode: 0644
```

> [!WARNING]
> Full volume directory mounts **mask (overwrite)** any existing files in `mountPath`. If you mount to `/etc/nginx`,
> existing default configuration files in that container directory will become inaccessible!

#### Step 2: Granular File Mount via `subPath`

To inject a single configuration file without obscuring other files in the destination directory, use `subPath`:

```yaml
volumeMounts:
  - name: config-vol
    mountPath: /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
    subPath: nginx.conf
volumes:
  - name: config-vol
    configMap:
      name: sample-service-config
```

